      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "C.H.U.D. (1984) epitomizes Reagan-era anxieties about urban decay and nuclear contamination through its grimy portrait of Manhattan's underground dwellers. Like <a href=\"/movie/22172\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"22172\">Street Trash</a> (1987) and <a href=\"/movie/27813\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"27813\">Basket Case</a> (1982), it captures the sleazy vitality of pre-gentrification New York City while delivering social commentary wrapped in B-movie thrills. The film's acronym title - Cannibalistic Humanoid Underground Dwellers - perfectly encapsulates the tongue-in-cheek approach to serious themes about governmental negligence and environmental disasters."
      },
      {
